codex
The generated semantics now has a concrete, material counterexample: both real Python implementations return `None` for `(9007199254740993, 9007199254740992)` because both operands round to the same binary64 value, while K returns the first integer by treating conversion as an exact rational. The same mismatch occurs for the numeric string `"9007199254740993"`. A separate valid scientific-notation string also crashes the generated LLVM semantics; I’m isolating that negative probe so the successful normal/boundary runs retain clean statuses.
